# Claude Code workspace dir (sessions, cache, local settings)
# Local Claude Code state stays out; the project skills are versioned,
# so an audit or a fix follows the same discipline in any clone.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# ...but a skill installed from elsewhere does not get versioned with
# them. `npx skills add` drops its payload in .agents/ and leaves a
# symlink here pointing into it, so committing the symlink would break
# in every other clone, and committing .agents/ would vendor
# third-party code into an AGPL tree without a licence review. The
# versioned-skills rule above is for THIS project's skills (audit,
# guard), which are a few KB of prose.
.claude/skills/security-audit
/.agents/
/skills-lock.json

# Compiled binaries (added after first commit mistake)
/bin/

# Brainstorming visual companion mockups
.superpowers/
